==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*gāną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ǵʰēh₁-||to leave}}.  The verb was defective in Germanic and may only have existed in the present tense.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|gān|lang=ofs}} (West Frisian {{term|gean|lang=fy}}), Old Saxon {{term/t|osx|gān}} (Saxon/Low German {{term|gan|lang=nds}}, {{term|gahn|lang=nds}}), Old Dutch {{term/t|odt|gān}} (Dutch {{term|gaan|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term/t|goh|gān}}, {{term/t|goh|gēn}} (German {{term|gehen|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|gá|lang=non}} (Danish and Swedish {{term|gå|lang=sv}}).

